{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/228318-canopic-jar-expectations-questions","id":228318,"title":"Canopic Jar Expectations, Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-14T12:20:30-07:00","id":228318,"title":"Canopic Jar Expectations, Questions","content":"Something I find surprising is how assumed the Arisen having access to all of their jars is. I get that an Arisen would treat them as its most important Relics, but many of the relics from Lost Irem are gone, and I get the vibe that they're easily broken/lost/stolen compared to larger, heavier stuff (like, say, a sarcophagus). I guess an Arisen is interred <i>with</i> their jars, but that doesn't seem a perfect solution. I dunno, do I have unrealistic expectations?<br /> <br /> Second question: in the case of the Twice-Arisen, that would imply that <i>all</i> of their Jars have been destroyed, but a new set will be made out of the, er...&quot;volunteer's&quot; organs, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T15:41:41-07:00","id":228520,"title":"","content":"I would assume that it's mostly down to not penalising the players for actions they don't have any say over. At least, not at character creation.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I got the same impression from the Twice-Arisen. New organs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:07:08-07:00","id":229594,"title":"","content":"For my PCs, I let them decide the location of one of their jars, while the other three placed elsewhere. For one PC, all jars but one were safe in her tomb. For another, each jar is hidden in one of their past tombs. I dont think, however, that the jars can be refilled even with a new body. the sahu and jars were created by the rite of return, and i doubt the jars can be remade. that being said, Im pretty sure you can resurrect a Mummy with any part of its corpse, even ashes. I did wonder about that--say, could a mummy cut off all their fingers and send them around the world as backup 'organs'? when a mummy who was risen from an organ dies, does it revert to the organ, or the full sahu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:06:37-07:00","id":229663,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty certain it's just the Canopic Jar Organs and their Talisman that can be used to resurrect themselves. If you want additional back-ups, the second tier of Rite of the Sacred Scarab exists for that purpose.<br /> <br /> As for the new organs, well, if you can claim a new body (and therefore sahu) without needing to re-enact the Rite of Return, is there a reason that body's sacred organs couldn't be extracted to fill new canopic jars? I never got the impression that it was the jars that were important, but rather the organs inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:46:26-07:00","id":230805,"title":"","content":"It is explicitly the organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T18:54:15-07:00","id":241903,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm not sure about that. The sidebar about the jars goes out of it's way to say that &quot;Mummies can be called in the presence of <i>any</i> part of their carcass&quot; - their emphasis, not mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T05:36:55-07:00","id":242177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/228318-canopic-jar-expectations-questions?p=241903#post241903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm not sure about that. The sidebar about the jars goes out of it's way to say that &quot;Mummies can be called in the presence of <i>any</i> part of their carcass&quot; - their emphasis, not mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be confusing wording, because the rest of the paragraph where your quote appears (page 152 in MtC for those looking for it) seems to imply that they're only talking about the other organs. And then at the bottom of the sidebar it says &quot;A mummy whose body <i>and</i> organs are destroyed utterly or inconveniently trapped has no other recourse but to try resurrecting within a stranger's remains.&quot; (emphasis theirs)<br /> <br /> So yeah, like Azahul said, I think there are only 6 backups: organs, Talisman, and Rite of the Sacred Scarab Tier 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T06:00:31-07:00","id":242191,"title":"","content":"Hm. I read it more like a general statement followed up by information about the canopic jars because the sidebar itself was about said jars. Whatever the case it's not as clear as it should be, and the fact it's not discussed outside of a casual mention in a sidebar is one of many editing and layout issues that aggravates me about Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T06:10:54-07:00","id":242203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/228318-canopic-jar-expectations-questions?p=242191#post242191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I read it more like a general statement followed up by information about the canopic jars because the sidebar itself was about said jars. Whatever the case it's not as clear as it should be, and the fact it's not discussed outside of a casual mention in a sidebar is one of many editing and layout issues that aggravates me about Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If we ever start a &quot;What do you want to see in Mummy 2nd Edition?&quot; thread my first response is going to be &quot;A better editor.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T17:36:32-07:00","id":242692,"title":"","content":"Tell me about it. I'm still frustrated that Rebuke the Vizier decided to spend time discussing how the third tier interacts with Mage and Vampire abilities, and entirely neglected to say whether or not it had an effect on Affinities.<br /> <br /> Regarding Canopic Jars though, from a thematic point of view it's so much more satisfying to have Mummies protecting their sacred organs than it is to have them scattering toes, fingers, and small scraps of flesh around the world to prevent their whole body being destroyed in one go. Outside of Four Jar Magic, having the resurrection rules apply to all parts of the Mummy's body effectively removes all value from the Canopic Jars. And what kind of Mummy game gives no importance to Canopic Jars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:02:11-07:00","id":243184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/228318-canopic-jar-expectations-questions?p=241903#post241903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm not sure about that. The sidebar about the jars goes out of it's way to say that &quot;Mummies can be called in the presence of <i>any</i> part of their carcass&quot; - their emphasis, not mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding (and I need to read back over to figure out what gave me this impression) was that the actual carcass (rather than the sahu) is damn near indestructible anyway, so the only way there could be &quot;parts&quot; would be if they were separated before the rite of return was performed. And since the only parts routinely separated pre-rite were the organs in the jars, it was something of a moot point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T15:02:29-07:00","id":243442,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;any part of their body&quot; thing basically means that if an active mummy is burned until all thats left is a finger, you can rezz from that. I do wonder if a mummy is rezzed from an organ then dies, if it reverts to an organ or stays a full khat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}